  "description": "OMENEB crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C204 H292 N12 Ni6 O80 Yb8,2(C4 H10 O1),6(C2 H6 O1),10(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 10 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Yb1A (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb2A (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb3A (Yb) has 9 O neighbors; Yb4A (Yb) has 10 O neighbors; Ni1A (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni2A (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni3A (Ni) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a branched tree with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.482-4.188 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.31-113.98°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Yb8Ni6L6(OAc)24(EtOH)6(H2O)2]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 24 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
